class Solution {
    public boolean searchMatrix(int[][] matrix, int target) {

        int rows = matrix.length;
        int cols = matrix[0].length;

        int low = 0;
        int high = rows * cols - 1;

        while (low <= high) {

            int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;

            // Convert 1D index to 2D position
            int row = mid / cols;
            int col = mid % cols;

            if (matrix[row][col] == target) {
                return true;
            } 
            else if (matrix[row][col] < target) {
                low = mid + 1;
            } 
            else {
                high = mid - 1;
            }
        }

        return false;
    }
}

/*
### 🧠 What you should remember

```text
2D sorted matrix
       ↓
Imagine it as 1D
       ↓
Binary Search
       ↓
row = mid / cols
col = mid % cols
```

**Time:** `O(log(m × n))`
**Space:** `O(1)`

Most importantly, you discovered the approach yourself rather than just memorizing the code. That's exactly how we'll handle your future LeetCode problems. 🚀
